{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkmyRJwgsaLzNcqc8MZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As far as I know, Vitest has no global CLI flag that repeats every test. Repetition is a per-test option: `test('name', { repeats: 10 }, () => { ... })`, or `describe('suite', { repeats: 10 }, ...)`, runs the test that many extra times and fails if any run fails.\n\nTo repeat the whole suite from the CLI, wrap it in a loop. For example, in PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\n1..20 | % { npx vitest run; if ($LASTEXITCODE) { break } }\n```\n\nTwo flags also help:\n\n- **`--sequence.shuffle`** randomizes test order, which exposes tests that depend on other tests.\n- **`--retry=3`** re-runs failing tests and reports the ones that pass on a later attempt as flaky.\n\nRun `npx vitest --help` to check whether your Vitest version has added a repeat flag."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2250,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2250},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffb8ae99-252e-4344-b39e-7bfcb1f54564","uuid":"2706e822-0fa5-46b5-9719-a470608768c5","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:17:31.727Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkmyAvzeDJssp77kc4D"}
